        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">This dataset includes a method of producing a lithium ion single cell. Lithium ion move from the cathode (LiMn2O4) into the electrolyte (LiPF6 in ethylenecarbonate) through the micropores of the sepeartor into the anode (lithium ion intercalation). During the charging phase. During the discharge of the battery the Li+-ions move back into the cathode.\n\n# Included processes\nThis dataset incudes the production of a single cell for a lithium ion battery. Cathode, anode and a seperator are calendared. An aluminium electrode tab is added. The singel cells are filled with electrolyte (LiPF6 in ethylencarbonate) in an inert atmosphere and packed up in a polyethylene envelope. For infrastructure, the ecoinvent dataset "chemical plant, organics" is accounted. Transportation efforts are based on ecoinvent standard estimates.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
